{"id": "EUVD-2026-103705", "enisaUuid": "9f838226-209e-3198-b3c7-de487289a5e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRISC-V: KVM: Serialize IMSIC attributes with vCPU migration\n\nKVM device ioctls are not serialized against KVM_RUN. As a result,\nkvm_riscv_aia_imsic_rw_attr() can snapshot the physical CPU and HGEI of\nan IMSIC VS-file before a concurrent vCPU migration releases it.\n\nThe HGEI can then be allocated to another vCPU before imsic_vsfile_rw()\nuses the stale tuple. A GET or SET attribute may consequently access the\nnew owner's interrupt file.\n\nSerialize the entire IMSIC attribute operation with the target vCPU\nmutex. This prevents the VS-file from being migrated and recycled until\nthe attribute access completes. Acquire the mutex killably so that the\ndevice ioctl remains interruptible while waiting for KVM_RUN to finish.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c2bcf6b173d4afed883cceea9d47f2c5194161d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a29c5d2dd2ef9a8617a9a6d5585696d5f149cd98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c525772c304c971b0d3a1f2898dedbae653efe90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71acbea44e78665ea90e3c310fca6bbdcc0252db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ae12ccaec6ec74945d8c1ef39f2c1b8df779abc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98465", "GHSA-95qg-qjx7-9h4r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3e66b426-8f00-301a-b30b-331c8caf63f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db8b7e97d6137a28b2bfc07e591d54da268f0c36 <a29c5d2dd2ef9a8617a9a6d5585696d5f149cd98"}, {"id": "483d23f8-6176-3f2b-8249-c0e27536df88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db8b7e97d6137a28b2bfc07e591d54da268f0c36 <8ae12ccaec6ec74945d8c1ef39f2c1b8df779abc"}, {"id": "5f40d5a8-4b73-3b80-8670-def8b4cf167b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "75716ba7-549a-360e-9b71-f6adefdf5f26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db8b7e97d6137a28b2bfc07e591d54da268f0c36 <6c2bcf6b173d4afed883cceea9d47f2c5194161d"}, {"id": "8079870d-9619-34c1-aab5-d05b0aa6a825", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "a2760d0a-fe2b-3aec-b8f4-5817873cbda8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "b7fcbce7-7f7d-3559-9a67-60d78623cf88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db8b7e97d6137a28b2bfc07e591d54da268f0c36 <c525772c304c971b0d3a1f2898dedbae653efe90"}, {"id": "bc6f4f53-4085-3c25-be61-114b765b35ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "ce2a3203-a1f7-39e6-bf7b-eb30edd3eb9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e358407c-a8a0-31c3-a7b9-7695e8a1e2f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "e8624870-6562-31f0-b9dc-33754c70fd85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db8b7e97d6137a28b2bfc07e591d54da268f0c36 <71acbea44e78665ea90e3c310fca6bbdcc0252db"}, {"id": "f9be9d20-7fd4-38d1-8dd8-719820a26000", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "04a0bb2f-10fd-3d7c-98af-789395b7164c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}